{"kind":"event","event_id":4156,"event_uid":"01M2K2P6G53TFYP1548FWH61YS","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.metadata_updated","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":199,"issue_uid":"01M2K2MYH485Q5PYCE545P89SK","issue_short_id":"89sk","actor":"impl:1@run-148","hlc_physical_ms":1789494237701,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"e91229ff693e7ba03fa4aa3d42a6f26d9df9f6ec257b2aa8bf4a99763c3ef4ee","payload":{"diff":{"work.attention":{"from":null,"to":"ok"}},"revision_new":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-15T17:43:57.701Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T17:43:57.701Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4181,"event_uid":"01M2K2Y50TPPJ5QB4PAX1XZX41","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":199,"issue_uid":"01M2K2MYH485Q5PYCE545P89SK","issue_short_id":"89sk","actor":"exam:1@run-148","hlc_physical_ms":1789494498330,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"4a0f46314ecbea0db1353753b8a8cf91b411d0df3d46c82049c0c9bb80cf5921","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K2Y50SJ6JAMCXNQVWYNJMJ","author":"exam:1@run-148","body":"Examiner (exam-1) starting: fleet/tests/test_engine_coverage.mjs, written where the Proof names it (no EXAM PATHS line).\n\nApproach, leg by leg:\n- (a)(b)(c)(d)(i)(j) call `engineCoverage` directly against scratch git trees built under a realpath'd mkdtemp: a stub `fleet/run-engine.mjs` whose first line carries three em dashes (so every later byte offset differs from its string index), an `if (false)` dead block inside `a()` for leg (j), a `b()` no sim calls, and a spare top-level line whose deletion is leg (b)'s pure-deletion head. One tree per head, so no checkout ordering is implied; line numbers are computed from unique markers in the stub text rather than hardcoded, and asserted with deepEqual.\n- (e)(f) drive `runEngine` through `rig` with `extraArgs: { width: 1 }` over a scratch repo holding the stub engine plus two stub sims written zed-then-alpha; the canned implementer edits `fleet/run-engine.mjs` (one line in `a()`, one in `b()`), so the first run's `engineCoverage` is non-null with a non-empty `unreached` beside `tests.passed: true` and `coverage.complete: true`. Two more runs for the null cases.\n- (h) reads `fleet/CONTRACT.md` and `skills/ultrapowers/references/report-format.md` in-process with the same range-then-match semantics the third and fourth `Run:` lines have, so the sim says what those lines say.\n- (g) is the bridge's own second `Run:` line; a sim may not spawn pytest (test_sims_are_hermetic M4), so it is not encodable inside the exam file — it will be returned under `unsatisfiable` as a leg the Proof's Run: line delivers, not as a gap in coverage.\n\nThe exam itself makes no spawn call: git goes through `gitSync` from `_engine_helpers.mjs`, the fixture sims are named only in `fs` writes, and `node` is spawned only by the implementation under test.","created_at":"2026-09-15T17:48:18.329246691Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T17:48:18.33Z"}
{"kind":"event","event_id":4229,"event_uid":"01M2K32YY0QH7B3A7R6HDYZMJH","origin_instance_uid":"01M29GPTT4YE7ZYSCW8FVMKZ1J","type":"issue.commented","project_id":31,"project_uid":"01M2HBYF26YQWA0S07E1J3NSGF","project_name":"popmechanic-ultrapowers","issue_id":199,"issue_uid":"01M2K2MYH485Q5PYCE545P89SK","issue_short_id":"89sk","actor":"impl:1@run-148","hlc_physical_ms":1789494655936,"hlc_counter":0,"content_hash":"a1fdc1fee69470519895c02e66e770991b2a62bc3c1f247d6a166b40385e9524","payload":{"comment_uid":"01M2K32YXZS4P8MPWGRDK0NYKZ","author":"impl:1@run-148","body":"Task 1 landed: `fleet/engine-coverage.mjs` (diff -U0 hunk parse → changed new-side lines; sims spawned as `node <tree>/<sim>` with cwd=tree and a fresh `NODE_V8_COVERAGE` mkdtemp each, pooled at `width`; V8 ranges read only from script entries whose `url` is exactly the file:// URL of `<tree>/<file>` — plus its realpath, so a symlinked temp root still matches while a copy at another path never does; count at a line = innermost (narrowest) containing range at the line's first character, offsets taken as JS string indices via a \\n scan of the file text). One call site in `runEngine` beside `coverage`, guarded by `git diff --name-only <baseSha> HEAD -- fleet/run-engine.mjs` and a readdir for `test_run_engine_*.mjs` sorted by path, wrapped in try/catch so a reading that cannot be taken is `null` and never a red. One report key `engineCoverage`. Docs: CONTRACT evidence sub-bullet + report-format row between `coverage` and `missingDeliverables`. Decision worth keeping: coverage temp dirs are deliberately NOT removed — the reading records nothing about them, and leg (i) reads each sim's own `NODE_V8_COVERAGE` value back from a file it wrote.","created_at":"2026-09-15T17:50:55.935816171Z"},"created_at":"2026-09-15T17:50:55.936Z"}
